Package: secubox-antirootkit
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, auditd, debsums, sudo, nftables, python3, python3-fastapi | python3-pip
Recommends: aide, rkhunter, chkrootkit
Description: SecuBox Anti-Rootkit - host-IDS anti-escape + exec scanner
 Host-based intrusion detection, v1 scope. LIVE: an auditd-fed
 exec-surveillance scanner that jails unknown/non-dpkg-backed executables
 into an egress-blocked cgroup (anti-escape), an append-only exec forensic
 log, a web panel, and an alert-only manual quarantine workflow (never
 auto-deletes or auto-chmods a suspect binary — it only emits an
 operator-reviewable plan).
 .
 Targeted auditd watches (low volume by design) cover the common unbacked
 exec surface: /usr/local/bin, /usr/local/sbin, /tmp, /dev/shm, /opt,
 /usr/lib/jvm and /home.
 .
 SCAFFOLDED (v1.1 follow-up, not yet scheduled): debsums/aide/rkhunter/
 chkrootkit integrity scanning — the wrapper module (api/integrity.py) and
 the Recommends below exist, but no timer wires it up automatically yet.
